 phase in humans</article-title><source>Am J Physiol Endocrinol Metab </source><year>2004</year><volume>287</volume><fpage>E174</fpage><lpage>E181</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15039146</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1152/ajpendo.00385.2003</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Burgess</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Crowley</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Gazda</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Fogg</surname><given-names>LF</given-names></name><name><surname>Eastman</surname><given-names>CI</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Preflight adjustment to eastward travel: 3 days of advancing sleep with and without morning bright light</article-title><source>J Biol Rhythms</source><year>2003</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>318</fpage><lpage>328</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12932084</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1177/0748730403253585</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Benloucif</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Guico</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Wolfe</surname><given-names>LF</given-names></name><name><surname>L'Hermite-Baleriaux</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Zee</surname><given-names>PC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effect of increasing light intensity vs. increasing light duration on phase shifts of the circadian clock of humans</article-title><source>Sleep</source><year>2003</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>A103</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mitchell</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoese</surname><given-names>EK</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Fogg</surname><given-names>LF</given-names></name><name><surname>Eastman</surname><given-names>CI</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Conflicting bright light exposure during night shifts impedes circadian adaptation</article-title><source>J Biol Rhythms</source><year>1997</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>5</fpage><lpage>15</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9104686</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1177/074873049701200103</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yang</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Spielman</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>D'Ambrosio</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Serizawa</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Nunes</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Birnbaum</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A single dose of melatonin prevents the phase delay associated with a delayed weekend sleep pattern</article-title><source>Sleep</source><year>2001</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>272</fpage><lpage>281</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11322709</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Wright</surname><given-names>HR</given-names></name><name><surname>Lack</surname><given-names>LC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sleeping-in on the weekend delays circadian phase and increases sleepiness the following week</article-title><source>Sleep and Biological Rhythms</source><year>2008</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>172</fpage><lpage>179</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1479-8425.2008.00356.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Burgess</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Eastman</surname><given-names>CI</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A late wake time phase delays the human dim light melatonin rhythm</article-title><source>Neurosci Lett</source><year>2006</year><volume>395</volume><fpage>191</fpage><lpage>195</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16309837</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.neulet.2005.10.082</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Burgess</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Eastman</surname><given-names>CI</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Early versus late bedtimes phase shift the human dim light melatonin rhythm despite a fixed morning lights on time</article-title><source>Neurosci Lett</source><year>2004</year><volume>356</volume><fpage>115</fpage><lpage>118</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14746877</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.neulet.2003.11.032</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dawson</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Encel</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Lushington</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Improving adaptation to simulated night shift: Timed exposure to bright light versus daytime melatonin administration</article-title><source>Sleep</source><year>1995</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>11</fpage><lpage>21</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7761738</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Campbell</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effects of times bright-light exposure on shift-work adaptation in middle-aged su